<%# The table's own totals: the three reasons the money is written under, then the sum.

    This was a separate "What this quarter pays" card sitting **below the Save grades button** and above
    the finalize block, which made the flow unreadable - a card after a save button reads as something
    the save produced, and nothing on it said whether it counted what you had just typed. Reported as
    exactly that.

    In the <tfoot> it cannot be ambiguous: it totals the column it sits under, and it is the element a
    screen reader expects a column summary in. That is also the invoice shape - line items, subtotals,
    total - which is what someone reading a spreadsheet expects, and it removes a card from a page that
    had too many.

    One element with an id, replaced whole on save, because every row of it is derived from the entries.
    Replacing the footer never touches the inputs, so it cannot take the cursor or a half-typed value
    with it.

    No rule above it: `divide-y` already separates rows and design.md's Dividers section forbids adding
    one where something else is already separating. The total row carries the weight instead. %>
<%= tag.tfoot id: "earnings-footer" do %>
  <% { attendance: "Attendance, including bonuses", math: "Math", reading: "Reading" }.each do |reason, label| %>
    <tr class="table-body-row">
      <th scope="row" class="table-body-cell text-left font-normal text-slate-600" colspan="5">
        <%= label %>
      </th>
      <td class="table-body-cell table-body-cell-right text-slate-600">
        <%= number_to_currency(earnings.totals_by_reason[reason] / 100.0) %>
      </td>
    </tr>
  <% end %>

  <tr class="table-body-row">
    <th scope="row" class="table-body-cell text-left font-medium text-slate-900" colspan="5">
      Total for <%= pluralize(earnings.student_count, "student") %>
    </th>
    <td class="table-body-cell table-body-cell-right font-semibold text-slate-900"
        data-testid="earnings-total">
      <%= number_to_currency(earnings.total_cents / 100.0) %>
    </td>
  </tr>
<% end %>
